WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.571
Step two runs Chapter
12's request check on

2
00:00:02.571 --> 00:00:05.113
three approved requests for new workloads.

3
00:00:05.113 --> 00:00:10.187
The domain has no G M S A yet, so
there's nothing to certify or retire.

4
00:00:10.187 --> 00:00:13.213
Two requests pass: timesheet and visitor.

5
00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:14.225
One is held.

6
00:00:14.225 --> 00:00:15.763
Step three reads why.

7
00:00:15.763 --> 00:00:18.968
Its name is nineteen characters
before the dollar sign,

8
00:00:18.968 --> 00:00:20.850
and the standard allows fifteen.

9
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:24.613
And it names only one owner, where
the standard needs exactly two.

10
00:00:24.613 --> 00:00:27.600
SailPoint approved it, and
the code still holds it.

11
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.575
The approvers decide on
the purpose and the risk;

12
00:00:30.575 --> 00:00:34.970
the code checks the standard, field
by field, before anything is created.
